                                                "text": "The name Shakespeare occurs from the 13th century on in the records of various English counties. The first Shakespeare as yet discovered in Warwickshire is one Thomas, a felon, who fled from the law in 1359. Toward the end of the fourteenth century there were landed Shakespeares at Baddesley, and this family held its own into the sixteenth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56cf86ff-2b2f-3eff-a47d-c6dcd4423c7a",
                                        "entry_id": "168bab88-543b-3d6b-b8df-97d69607b4bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "William Shakespeare, an English playwright and poet of the late sixteenth and early seventeenth centuries."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cbb21eb3-9dee-3f63-a4d2-f17f7bf32eff",
                                        "entry_id": "168bab88-543b-3d6b-b8df-97d69607b4bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "His works or media adaptations of his works."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6d9fba7-e278-43c2-af65-50d64d965659",
                                                "sense_id": "cbb21eb3-9dee-3f63-a4d2-f17f7bf32eff",
                                                "text": "He is reading Shakespeare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "788b7186-9294-4e0d-87af-af596455d965",
                                                "sense_id": "cbb21eb3-9dee-3f63-a4d2-f17f7bf32eff",
                                                "text": "I'm surprised that even the allusion to Hamlet flew over his head. Even someone who barely knows Shakespeare might catch that one!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22309249-69bb-367d-ab62-2e134be9fbec",
                                        "entry_id": "168bab88-543b-3d6b-b8df-97d69607b4bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place name:",
                                            "A village in Perth East township, Ontario, Canada, named after the playwright."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2513631-7fd4-330c-9dce-8965bcf9ef05",
                                        "entry_id": "168bab88-543b-3d6b-b8df-97d69607b4bf",
